# React Meta Framework Patterns

**Authoritative doc:** [Create an app with the meta framework](https://developers.freshworks.com/docs/app-sdk/v3.0/common/app-development-process/create-an-app-with-the-meta-framework/)

**When to use:** Any new UI app (default) or vanilla JS → React migration. Vanilla JS + Crayons is **opt-in only** when the user explicitly requests it.

## Default stack

| Layer | Default | Notes |
|-------|---------|-------|
| Framework | **Meta (`metaConfig.framework: "react"`)** | In `manifest.json`, not a separate file |
| UI | **`@freshworks/dew-components`** + **`@freshworks/dew-styles`** | **Required** — see `dew-components.md` and [Storybook](https://dew.freshworkscorp.com/dew-3.0/) |
| React | **19+** preferred | Functional and class components both supported |
| Routing | **React Router** — `path="*"` home, `/app/...` feature routes | Official Meta sample pattern |
| TypeScript | Optional `.tsx` / `tsconfig.json` | Supported |

## Forbidden in Meta workflow

- `@freshworks/crayons`, Crayons CDN, `<fw-*>` web components
- Plain HTML form controls as primary UI (use DEW React components)
- `metaConfig` outside `manifest.json`
- **`<DewTheme>` as a JSX wrapper** — `DewTheme` is a Tailwind config export, not a React component (causes blank UI / invalid element type)

## Allowed alongside DEW

Tailwind CSS, PostCSS, MUI, Redux, React Router extras, date-fns, axios (manifest-pinned), and other third-party packages **when the user asks or reference patterns apply**. Do **not** remove these during validate/fix unless they break Platform 3.0 rules.

## manifest.json (Meta)

```json
{
  "platform-version": "3.0",
  "modules": { ... },
  "metaConfig": {
    "framework": "react",
    "packageManager": "npm"
  },
  "engines": { "node": "24.11.0", "fdk": "10.1.0" }
}
```

- **`metaConfig.framework`**: required `"react"`
- **`metaConfig.packageManager`**: optional (`npm` default)
- Meta apps: minimum **FDK 10.1.0** in `engines.fdk`

## Directory layout

```
app/
├── index.html              # At app root (name configurable in manifest location.url)
├── icon.svg                # Or path declared in manifest
├── index.jsx               # Entry (bundled by FDK Vite)
├── mount.jsx               # ErrorBoundary + createRoot (react-error-boundary)
├── components/
├── public/
└── styles/
config/
test/
manifest.json
package.json
vite.config.js              # Optional (FDK 10.1.5+)
```

**Custom iparams (optional):** `config/iparams.html` + `config/assets/` — see **`custom-iparams.md`**. Do **not** nest manifest HTML under `app/components/` or `app/scripts/`.

## Custom HTML

- **`#root`** mount point in shell HTML
- **`{{{appclient}}}`** when app uses Data method, Request method, Installation settings, Data store, or SMI — see `references/react-meta/custom-html.md`
- Multi-placeholder: one HTML shell per surface (e.g. `index.html`, `ticketSidebar.html`)

## React Router

```jsx
<Route path="*" element={<Home />} />
<Route path="/app/demo" element={<DemoPage />} />
```

Home/fallback **must** use `path="*"`. Feature routes use **`/app/...`** prefix.

## vite.config.js (optional)

- Location: **project root**
- FDK **deep-merges** developer config with internal Vite config
- **FDK wins** on conflict: entry points, `app` / `config` resolve aliases, FDK-required plugins
- Safe extensions: extra aliases, PostCSS/Tailwind, `define`, `server.proxy`, `manualChunks`
- See `references/react-meta/vite-config.md`

## Scaffold commands

| Action | Command / template |
|--------|-------------------|
| Create (default UI) | `/fdk-react-create` or `fdk create --template react-starter-template` |
| Migrate vanilla → Meta | `/fdk-react-migrate` |
| Vanilla opt-in | `assets/templates/frontend-skeleton/` (Crayons) |

## Skeleton templates

| Template | Path |
|----------|------|
| React Meta frontend | `assets/templates/react-meta-frontend-skeleton/` |
| React Meta hybrid | `assets/templates/react-meta-hybrid-skeleton/` |
| React Meta OAuth | `assets/templates/react-meta-oauth-skeleton/` |
| Custom iparams (React Settings) | `assets/templates/react-meta-custom-iparams-skeleton/` |

